-- FIX-1 (end-of-sprint review S0-2 / #1959): a structured body goal that the
-- enclosing DECLARED context does not entail must REJECT, not defer.
--
-- Hand-derived from DICT-SEMANTICS §4.2 BEFORE running anything.  "Defer" means
-- "forward this predicate outward to the binder that quantifies its variables,
-- and let each use site discharge it".  `g`'s binder is a SIGNATURE, and a
-- signature is FIXED: it carries `Tag (Wrap a)` and nothing else.  The body's
-- second goal `Tag (Box a)` can therefore never be forwarded anywhere, so
-- deferring it means DROPPING it -- and `main = println (g 'z')` has no
-- `impl Tag (Box Char)` to drop to.  The only sound verdict is a located reject
-- at the `tagOf (Box x)` occurrence.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS PINS.  At the pre-fix sprint head `aa36d555`, on this tree, cold
-- built: check 0 with ZERO diagnostics and the scheme `g : Tag Wrap a => a ->
-- String`, run 1 (`E-PANIC: unknown op '+'`), build 0 with the SHIPPED BINARY
-- PRINTING `wrapChar|boxInt=123` -- `impl Tag (Box Int)`'s body evaluating
-- `n + 1` over the Char `'z'` (ASCII 122).  A type-confused dict at exit 0.
-- Stable at -O0/-O1/-O2 (hand-linked from `--keep-ir`), so not #1958's UB.
--
-- ⚠️ THE FIRST COMPONENT IS LOAD-BEARING AND MUST STAY.  `tagOf (Wrap x)` IS the
-- declared context and must keep deferring; only the `Box` half is illegal.  A
-- gate that rejected both would false-reject
-- `s-structured-carry-declared-context-kept.mdk` and
-- `s-instantiated-reselect-declared.mdk`, the ACCEPT siblings of this widening.
-- The discrimination is by tyvar-cell IDENTITY (`monoSameGiven`), not by
-- interface name: both goals are at `Tag`, on the same variable, and only the
-- structural shape tells them apart.
--
-- ⚠️ VERDICT AND CODE, NO LOCATION.
data Wrap a = Wrap a

data Box a = Box a

interface Tag t where
  tagOf : t -> String

impl Tag (Wrap Int) where
  tagOf _ = "wrapInt"

impl Tag (Wrap Char) where
  tagOf _ = "wrapChar"

impl Tag (Box Int) where
  tagOf (Box n) = "boxInt=\{n + 1}"

g : Tag (Wrap a) => a -> String
g x = "\{tagOf (Wrap x)}|\{tagOf (Box x)}"

main = println (g 'z')
